% Goal

Implement and maintain `brain/api/api_plan_order.py` as the POST {track_ids[], base_rev} is a FULL REPLACEMENT, never index arithmetic, because index deltas desync the moment two writers interleave. POST {move_bunch, to_index, base_rev} moves a bunch as a unit. Rejects a body that is not a permutation of the current selection, which is what structurally prevents this route from adding or removing tracks (that is module 25's job). An order that breaks an active bunch is a 422 NAMING THE GROUP: 422 and 409 are both used on this one route and are not interchangeable, because 409 means the plan moved underneath you and repeating may succeed, while 422 means the body was understood and the constraint is unsatisfiable so repeating it unchanged will fail identically. Calls transition_overrides.reconcile in the SAME write so orphaning is atomic with the reorder. Appends EXACTLY ONE journal entry per accepted write with rev_before/rev_after and a detail summarizing the move plus any transitions reconcile orphaned; a 422 or 409 appends nothing.

% Product contract

- Preserve the exact public interface declared in `<pdd-interface>`.
- Treat the reviewed architecture description in this prompt as normative behavior.
- Keep plan identity, immutable track identity, revision guards, and non-destructive storage semantics intact across GUI, CLI, and agent callers.
- Preserve compatible behavior outside this module's stated responsibility; do not redesign unrelated mixing or playback logic.
- Reject malformed, stale, ambiguous, or unsafe writes explicitly instead of silently losing plan data.
- Keep the implementation deterministic where the contract describes deterministic behavior.
- Target Python 3.13+ for Python modules and baseline browser JavaScript without a bundler for browser modules.
- Inspect the current implementation, its declared dependency modules, and the focused tests before changing code. This is a brownfield source prompt: working, tested behavior not contradicted here remains part of the contract.

% Architecture detail

POST {track_ids[], base_rev} is a FULL REPLACEMENT, never index arithmetic, because index deltas desync the moment two writers interleave. POST {move_bunch, to_index, base_rev} moves a bunch as a unit. Rejects a body that is not a permutation of the current selection, which is what structurally prevents this route from adding or removing tracks (that is module 25's job). An order that breaks an active bunch is a 422 NAMING THE GROUP: 422 and 409 are both used on this one route and are not interchangeable, because 409 means the plan moved underneath you and repeating may succeed, while 422 means the body was understood and the constraint is unsatisfiable so repeating it unchanged will fail identically. Calls transition_overrides.reconcile in the SAME write so orphaning is atomic with the reorder. Appends EXACTLY ONE journal entry per accepted write with rev_before/rev_after and a detail summarizing the move plus any transitions reconcile orphaned; a 422 or 409 appends nothing.

